# Directed FU test: simultaneous completion on limited writeback ports.
# The first print serializes the machine, draining the warm-up store's
# cache miss so the trio below runs with deterministic latencies. Then
# mul (latency 3, issued first), lw (address generation + 1-cycle hit,
# issued second) and addi (latency 1, issued third) all complete in
# the same cycle — three results, two writeback ports. The two oldest
# (mul, lw) write back; the addi holds its ALU's output slot one cycle
# ("wb port conflict"). Values must still come out right.
# Expected output: 5 then 27, exit 0.
00300093   # addi x1, x0, 3
00500113   # addi x2, x0, 5
10000313   # addi x6, x0, 256
00232023   # sw   x2, 0(x6)       park 5 in memory (cold miss, warms the line)
00010513   # addi x10, x2, 0
00100893   # addi x17, x0, 1      syscall 1: print integer
00000073   # ecall                prints 5; serializes, miss fully drained
022081B3   # mul  x3, x1, x2      15, completes in 3 cycles
00032203   # lw   x4, 0(x6)       5, hit: completes 2 cycles after issue
00700293   # addi x5, x0, 7       completes 1 cycle after issue
004183B3   # add  x7, x3, x4      20
005383B3   # add  x7, x7, x5      27
00038513   # addi x10, x7, 0
00100893   # addi x17, x0, 1
00000073   # ecall                prints 27
00000513   # addi x10, x0, 0
05D00893   # addi x17, x0, 93     syscall 93: exit
00000073   # ecall
